"""Scene definitions for the XML External Entities and Template Injection teaching video (generated from concept.toml)."""

SCENES = [
    dict(key='01-poster', kind='poster', title='XML External Entities and Template Injection',
         body=None,
         narration="Hello, and welcome. [[slnc 400]] This video explains X M L external entities, or X X E, and server-side template injection, or S S T I, in Java. [[slnc 300]] X M L stands for extensible markup language: text with nested tags. [[slnc 300]] This video is presented by Jayasekhar Konduru. [[slnc 600]] First, a simple definition. [[slnc 300]] An X M L parser and a template engine both follow instructions that they find in their input. [[slnc 300]] An X M L file can tell the parser to read a file from the server. [[slnc 300]] And a template can tell the engine to run an expression. [[slnc 300]] If an attacker writes the input, the attacker writes the instructions. [[slnc 600]] Think of a form whose small print says: attach a copy of whatever is in the manager's drawer. [[slnc 300]] A careful clerk ignores the small print. [[slnc 300]] A careless one obeys it. [[slnc 600]] Our example is an online store."),
    dict(key='02-scenario', kind='bullets', title='The Scenario',
         body=['An online store accepts supplier invoices', 'as XML files.', '', 'It sends customers e-mails from templates,', "with the customer's name filled in.", '', "The demo uses the JDK's own XML parser.", 'Every secret in it is fake.'],
         narration="Here is the scenario. [[slnc 400]] An online store accepts invoices from its suppliers, as small X M L files. [[slnc 500]] It also sends its customers e-mails from templates, with each customer's name filled in. [[slnc 600]] The demo uses the X M L parser that comes with the Java development kit, and a small template engine written for the demo. [[slnc 300]] A temporary file stands in for a secret file on the server, and every secret in the demo is fake."),
    dict(key='03-words', kind='bullets', title='The Words',
         body=['Entity: a name the parser replaces by a value', 'DOCTYPE: the part of a file that defines entities', 'External entity: its value is a file or an address', 'Template: a text with holes for values', 'Expression: a path the engine works out, ${a.b}', 'Escaping: special characters made harmless'],
         narration='Before the demos, the words. [[slnc 500]] An entity is a name, in an X M L file, that the parser replaces by a value. [[slnc 500]] The doctype is the part at the top of a file that may define entities. [[slnc 500]] An external entity is one whose value is fetched from a file or an address. [[slnc 500]] A template is a text with holes, filled with values. [[slnc 500]] An expression is a path, like dollar, brace, a dot b, that some engines work out at run time. [[slnc 500]] And escaping replaces special characters, so a value can only ever be text.'),
    dict(key='04-letters-1', kind='bullets', title='What the Letters Stand For',
         body=['XML: Extensible Markup Language: text with nested tags', 'XXE: XML External Entity: a file or address read through an entity', 'SSTI: Server-Side Template Injection: text that runs inside a template', 'DTD: Document Type Definition: the rules and entities a DOCTYPE declares', 'doctype, entity, system: XML words: start definitions; define a name; read from an address', 'JDK: Java Development Kit: Java with its standard library and tools'],
         narration="A few letters come up again and again, so here is what they stand for. [[slnc 400]] X M L is extensible markup language: text with nested tags, like an invoice tag that holds a customer and a total. [[slnc 400]] X X E is X M L external entity: an attack where an uploaded file makes the parser read a server file or an address. [[slnc 400]] S S T I is server-side template injection: text from a user that runs inside a template, on the server. [[slnc 400]] D T D is document type definition: the rules and entities that a doctype declares, inline or in an external file. [[slnc 400]] Doctype starts the definitions at the top of the file. Entity defines a name. System means the name's value is fetched from an address, like a file. [[slnc 400]] J D K is the Java development kit: Java, with its standard library, which includes an X M L parser."),
    dict(key='05-letters-2', kind='bullets', title='What the Letters Stand For (continued)',
         body=['SMTP: Simple Mail Transfer Protocol: how a program sends e-mail', 'HTML: HyperText Markup Language: the language of web pages and many e-mails'],
         narration="S M T P is simple mail transfer protocol: how a program sends e-mail. The shop's S M T P password is its mail password. [[slnc 400]] H T M L is hypertext markup language: the language of web pages, and of many e-mails."),
    dict(key='06-core', kind='figure', title='Two readers that obey their input',
         body='reader_obeys',
         narration="Let's see the whole idea on one picture. [[slnc 400]] At the top, an invoice upload. [[slnc 300]] The red part defines a name, x x e, as a file on the server, and the note uses that name. [[slnc 300]] The X M L parser does what the file says. [[slnc 300]] It opens the file, and the note becomes the server's secret. [[slnc 700]] At the bottom, an e-mail template. [[slnc 300]] The code pasted a customer's name into it, and the name, in red, is an expression. [[slnc 300]] The template engine does what the template says. [[slnc 300]] It works out the expression, and the e-mail shows the mail password. [[slnc 700]] Two different readers, one mistake. [[slnc 300]] Input written by an attacker was read as instructions. [[slnc 300]] The fixes: a parser that refuses the doctype, and an engine with no expressions."),
    dict(key='07-act-1-figure', kind='figure', title='An honest invoice: five lines in, three fields out',
         body='honest_upload',
         narration='First demo: an invoice upload. [[slnc 400]] On the left, the file the supplier sends. [[slnc 300]] An invoice, with a customer, a total and a note. [[slnc 700]] Look at the note. [[slnc 300]] It says: thanks, ampersand, a m p, semicolon, see you soon. [[slnc 300]] In X M L, a plain ampersand is not allowed. [[slnc 300]] So the file writes a name instead: amp. [[slnc 300]] That name is an entity. [[slnc 300]] The parser replaces it by its value, the ampersand character. [[slnc 700]] On the right, the result. [[slnc 300]] Three fields: Ana, forty-two fifty, and the note, with a real ampersand. [[slnc 500]] Keep this in mind: an entity is a name the parser replaces. [[slnc 300]] The next demo defines its own.'),
    dict(key='08-act-1', kind='console', title='Act One — An invoice upload',
         body='ONE. An invoice upload.\n  THE UPLOAD (the XML file the supplier sends):\n    <invoice>\n      <customer>Ana</customer>\n      <total>42.50</total>\n      <note>Thanks &amp; see you soon</note>\n    </invoice>\n  WHAT THE PARSER DOES:\n    &amp; is a built-in entity: it is replaced by &\n  THE RESULT (the fields the shop stores):\n    customer  Ana\n    total     42.50\n    note      Thanks & see you soon',
         narration='Here is the real output. [[slnc 400]] The upload: five lines of X M L. [[slnc 400]] What the parser does: it replaces the entity amp by an ampersand. [[slnc 400]] And the result: customer Ana, total forty-two fifty, and the note.'),
    dict(key='09-act-2-figure', kind='figure', title='A name for a server file, and a name that multiplies',
         body='entity_fetch',
         narration="Second demo: the parser reads what the file tells it to. [[slnc 400]] At the top, the upload. [[slnc 300]] Its first lines are a doctype. [[slnc 300]] They define a new entity, called x x e. [[slnc 300]] Its value is not text. [[slnc 300]] It is the address of a file, on the server. [[slnc 700]] The note says: ampersand, x x e. [[slnc 300]] So the parser opens that file, and puts its text into the note. [[slnc 300]] The shop stores the server's secret, and shows it back to the uploader. [[slnc 800]] Below, a second file: an entity bomb. [[slnc 300]] a zero is the word lol. [[slnc 300]] a one holds ten copies of a zero. [[slnc 300]] Each name holds ten of the name below it, six times. [[slnc 300]] Ten times ten, six times, is one million copies. [[slnc 300]] Three letters each: three million characters, from a file of a few hundred. [[slnc 600]] The parser stops it, but only because of the Java library's default limit."),
    dict(key='10-act-2-1', kind='console', title='Act Two — The parser reads what the file tells it to',
         body='TWO. The parser reads what the file tells it to.\n  THE UPLOAD (a DOCTYPE defines the entity xxe):\n    <!DOCTYPE invoice [\n      <!ENTITY xxe SYSTEM "file:///.../secret.txt">\n    ]>\n    <invoice><customer>Mallory</customer><total>1.00</total>\n      <note>&xxe;</note></invoice>\n  WHAT THE PARSER DOES:\n    opens the file that xxe names, on the server,\n    and puts its text where &xxe; stands\n  THE RESULT (the fields the shop stores):\n    customer  Mallory\n    total     1.00\n    note      demo-secret-from-the-server  <- A SERVER FILE',
         narration="Here is the output, one file per page. [[slnc 400]] The upload, with a doctype that defines x x e as a file on the server. [[slnc 400]] What the parser does: it opens the file, and puts its text where ampersand x x e stands. [[slnc 400]] The result: the note is the server's secret."),
    dict(key='11-act-2-2', kind='console', title='Act Two — The parser reads what the file tells it to',
         body='TWO. (continued)\n  THE UPLOAD (an entity bomb, 464 characters):\n    <!ENTITY a0 "lol">\n    <!ENTITY a1 "&a0;&a0;&a0;&a0;&a0;&a0;&a0;&a0;&a0;&a0;">\n    ... a2 to a5 the same way, ten of the level below\n    <!ENTITY a6 "&a5;&a5;&a5;&a5;&a5;&a5;&a5;&a5;&a5;&a5;">\n    <note>&a6;</note>\n  WHAT IT WOULD EXPAND TO (worked out):\n    a6 = 10 x 10 x 10 x 10 x 10 x 10 = 1,000,000 copies of lol\n    1,000,000 x 3 letters = 3,000,000 characters\n  THE RESULT:\n    refused: stopped by the parser\'s entity expansion limit\n  stopped by luck: the JDK\'s default limit, not our setting',
         narration="The entity bomb, four hundred and sixty-four characters. [[slnc 400]] Worked out: one million copies of lol, three million characters. [[slnc 400]] The result: refused, by the parser's expansion limit. [[slnc 300]] Stopped by luck, not by our settings."),
    dict(key='12-act-3-figure', kind='figure', title='One setting stops both attacks; the rest are extra layers',
         body='doctype_refused',
         narration='Third demo: refuse the doctype. [[slnc 400]] On the left, the settings of the safe parser. [[slnc 300]] They are read back from the code, not typed by hand. [[slnc 600]] The first one is the fix. [[slnc 300]] Disallow doctype declaration: true. [[slnc 300]] An invoice never needs a doctype, so any file that has one is refused. [[slnc 600]] The others are extra layers, in case someone turns the first one off later. [[slnc 300]] No external D T Ds, no external schemas, no X include, no entity expansion, and at most ten thousand characters. [[slnc 700]] On the right, the same files again. [[slnc 300]] The honest invoice is accepted. [[slnc 300]] The file entity and the bomb are refused for the same reason, at the first line. [[slnc 300]] And an oversized upload is refused before parsing.'),
    dict(key='13-act-3-1', kind='console', title='Act Three — Refuse the DOCTYPE',
         body='THREE. Refuse the DOCTYPE.\n  THE PARSER SETTINGS (read back from SafeInvoiceParser):\n    disallow-doctype-decl     true  <- THE FIX\n    secure processing         true\n    external DTDs allowed     "" (none)\n    external schemas allowed  "" (none)\n    XInclude                  false\n    expand entity references  false\n    largest upload            10,000 characters',
         narration='Here is the output. [[slnc 400]] The parser settings, read back from the safe parser. [[slnc 300]] The doctype is refused, and every external access is empty.'),
    dict(key='14-act-3-2', kind='console', title='Act Three — Refuse the DOCTYPE',
         body='THREE. (continued)\n  THE UPLOADS AND RESULTS (the same three files):\n    honest invoice\n      -> accepted: customer=Ana, total=42.50\n    external entity (file)\n      -> refused: a DOCTYPE is not allowed in an invoice\n    entity bomb\n      -> refused: a DOCTYPE is not allowed in an invoice\n    an invoice of 10,095 characters\n      -> refused: upload too large',
         narration='The same uploads. [[slnc 300]] The honest invoice: accepted. [[slnc 300]] The file entity and the bomb: a doctype is not allowed in an invoice. [[slnc 300]] And ten thousand and ninety-five characters: upload too large.'),
    dict(key='15-act-4-figure', kind='figure', title='The pasted name, one method call at a time',
         body='expression_walk',
         narration="Fourth demo: a template engine that evaluates expressions. [[slnc 400]] At the top, the template as the code built it. [[slnc 300]] The customer's name, in red, was pasted in. [[slnc 300]] The name is: dollar, brace, app dot config dot smtp password. [[slnc 700]] The engine reads the part between the braces as a path. [[slnc 300]] It starts at app, the running application. [[slnc 300]] Dot config calls the method config, and gets the settings. [[slnc 300]] Dot smtp password calls that method, and gets the mail password. [[slnc 700]] The second row is another name: customer dot class dot name. [[slnc 300]] It calls get class, then get name, and shows the Java class behind the data. [[slnc 300]] Any public method can be reached this way. [[slnc 600]] The e-mail says: hello, and the password."),
    dict(key='16-act-4-1', kind='console', title='Act Four — A template engine that evaluates expressions',
         body="FOUR. A template engine that evaluates expressions.\n  WHAT EVERY TEMPLATE CAN REACH (customer and app):\n    customer.name            Ana\n    customer.email           ana@example.test\n    app.version              3.4.1\n    app.config.smtpPassword  demo-smtp-password  <- SECRET\n  THE OWNER'S TEMPLATE:\n    Hello ${customer.name}, your order shipped.\n  THE RESULT:\n    Hello Ana, your order shipped.",
         narration="Here is the output. [[slnc 400]] What every template can reach: the customer, and the application, including the mail password. [[slnc 400]] The owner's template, and its result: hello Ana."),
    dict(key='17-act-4-2', kind='console', title='Act Four — A template engine that evaluates expressions',
         body="FOUR. (continued)\n  THE CUSTOMER'S NAME (typed at sign-up):\n    ${app.config.smtpPassword}\n  THE TEMPLATE AS BUILT (the name pasted in):\n    Hello ${app.config.smtpPassword}, your order shipped.\n  HOW THE ENGINE WORKS IT OUT (step by step):\n    app -> App\n    .config -> config() -> AppConfig\n    .smtpPassword -> smtpPassword() -> demo-smtp-password\n  THE RESULT:\n    Hello demo-smtp-password, your order shipped.  <- THE SECRET",
         narration="The customer's name. [[slnc 300]] The template as built, with the name pasted in. [[slnc 400]] How the engine works it out: app, then config, then smtp password. [[slnc 400]] The result: the secret, in the e-mail."),
    dict(key='18-act-4-3', kind='console', title='Act Four — A template engine that evaluates expressions',
         body='FOUR. (continued)\n  ANOTHER PASTED NAME:\n    ${customer.class.name}\n  HOW THE ENGINE WORKS IT OUT (step by step):\n    customer -> Customer\n    .class -> getClass() -> Class\n    .name -> getName() -> com.jk.explore.security.xmlinj.Customer\n  THE SAME NAME PASSED AS DATA (fixed template):\n    Hello ${customer.name}  name = ${app.config.smtpPassword}\n      -> Hello ${app.config.smtpPassword}\n  data is not evaluated twice; pasted text is',
         narration='Another pasted name: customer dot class dot name. [[slnc 300]] Get class, then get name: the full class name. [[slnc 500]] The same name, passed as data to a fixed template, stays text. [[slnc 300]] Data is not evaluated twice. [[slnc 300]] Pasted text is.'),
    dict(key='19-act-5-figure', kind='figure', title='Two holes, no expressions, every value escaped',
         body='logic_less',
         narration="Fifth demo: a logic-less engine keeps data as data. [[slnc 400]] Top left, the only holes it knows: name and email. [[slnc 300]] There is no path, no dot, no method call. [[slnc 700]] On the right, the same three templates. [[slnc 300]] The owner's template says hello Ana. [[slnc 300]] The pasted expression stays text, because this engine has no expressions. [[slnc 300]] And the name passed as data stays text too. [[slnc 700]] Below, a name with markup: a script tag. [[slnc 300]] Each special character is replaced by an entity. [[slnc 300]] Less than becomes ampersand l t. [[slnc 300]] Greater than becomes ampersand g t. [[slnc 300]] The result is shown as text, and never runs."),
    dict(key='20-act-5-1', kind='console', title='Act Five — A logic-less engine keeps data as data',
         body="FIVE. A logic-less engine keeps data as data.\n  THE VALUES (a flat list; nothing else is reachable):\n    {{name}}    {{email}}\n  WHAT THE ENGINE DOES:\n    fills each {{hole}} from the list, escaped, in one pass\n  THE TEMPLATES AND RESULTS:\n    the owner's template\n      -> Hello Ana, your order shipped.\n    the name pasted into the template\n      -> Hello ${app.config.smtpPassword}, your order shipped.\n    the name passed as data\n      -> Hello ${app.config.smtpPassword}",
         narration="Here is the output. [[slnc 400]] The values: two named holes. [[slnc 300]] What the engine does: it fills each hole from the list, escaped, in one pass. [[slnc 400]] The owner's template: hello Ana. [[slnc 300]] The pasted name and the name passed as data both stay text."),
    dict(key='21-act-5-2', kind='console', title='Act Five — A logic-less engine keeps data as data',
         body='FIVE. (continued)\n  THE NAME (with markup):\n    <script>x</script>\n  HOW EACH CHARACTER IS ESCAPED (for HTML):\n    & -> &amp;   < -> &lt;   > -> &gt;\n    " -> &quot;   \' -> &#39;\n  THE RESULT (Hello {{name}}):\n    Hello &lt;script&gt;x&lt;/script&gt;',
         narration='The name with markup. [[slnc 300]] How each character is escaped. [[slnc 300]] And the result: the script tag, as harmless text.'),
    dict(key='22-costs', kind='bullets', title='What It Costs',
         body=['Some XML really needs a DOCTYPE', 'Every parser library has its own settings', 'Logic-less templates are less convenient', 'Escaping depends on where the value goes', 'Template authors must be trusted people'],
         narration='Nothing is free. [[slnc 400]] Here is what the defences cost. [[slnc 500]] Some X M L formats really need a doctype, and then the other parser settings carry the whole load. [[slnc 500]] Every parser library has its own settings, so each one in the project has to be checked. [[slnc 500]] Logic-less templates are less convenient: the code prepares every value in advance. [[slnc 500]] Escaping depends on where a value goes, H T M L, a link, or plain text. [[slnc 300]] And whoever writes the templates must be a trusted person, because the template is code.'),
    dict(key='23-verdict', kind='bullets', title='How To Use It',
         body=['XML from outside: refuse the DOCTYPE', '  and switch off external entities', "Test every parser's settings", 'Templates are fixed files with named holes', 'Customer text is data, never template', 'Escape every value for where it goes'],
         narration="So, how do you use it? [[slnc 400]] Parse X M L from outside with the doctype refused, and with external entities and external schemas switched off as extra layers. [[slnc 500]] Test the settings of every parser in the project, because each library has its own. [[slnc 500]] Write templates as fixed files with named holes. [[slnc 500]] Never paste a customer's text into a template: pass it in as data. [[slnc 300]] And escape every value for the place it goes."),
    dict(key='24-classes', kind='bullets', title='The Java Classes',
         body=["NaiveInvoiceParser: the first version: the JDK's XML parser as it comes", 'SafeInvoiceParser: the fix: no DOCTYPE, no external access, a size limit', 'ExpressionEngine: the first template engine: ${a.b.c} walked by reflection', 'XmlTemplateDemo: runs the five acts, and makes the mistake behind SSTI', 'LogicLessEngine: the fix: two named holes, escaped values, one pass'],
         narration='Now, a quick look at the code. [[slnc 300]] The X M L parser is the one in the Java development kit, so the attack is real. [[slnc 300]] The template engines are small classes written for the demo. [[slnc 300]] Here are the lines that matter.'),
    dict(key='25-class-1', kind='code', title='NaiveInvoiceParser — the default factory',
         body="// NaiveInvoiceParser: the first version: the JDK's XML parser as it comes\nprotected DocumentBuilderFactory factory() {\n    return DocumentBuilderFactory.newInstance();",
         narration='The first version takes the parser factory with its defaults. [[slnc 300]] The defaults read a doctype, and fetch external entities, for whoever wrote the file.'),
    dict(key='26-class-2', kind='code', title='SafeInvoiceParser — refuse the DOCTYPE, then extra layers',
         body='// SafeInvoiceParser: the fix: no DOCTYPE, no external access, a size limit\nf.setFeature("http://apache.org/xml/features/disallow-doctype-decl", true);\nf.setFeature(XMLConstants.FEATURE_SECURE_PROCESSING, true);\nf.setAttribute(XMLConstants.ACCESS_EXTERNAL_DTD, "");\nf.setAttribute(XMLConstants.ACCESS_EXTERNAL_SCHEMA, "");\nf.setXIncludeAware(false);\nf.setExpandEntityReferences(false);',
         narration='The fix is the first line: refuse any doctype. [[slnc 300]] The other lines are extra layers: no external D T Ds or schemas, no X include, and no entity expansion. [[slnc 300]] The demo reads these settings back and prints them.'),
    dict(key='27-class-3', kind='code', title='SafeInvoiceParser — a size limit before parsing',
         body='// SafeInvoiceParser: the fix: no DOCTYPE, no external access, a size limit\nif (xml.length() > MAX_BYTES) {\n    throw new InvoiceException("upload too large");',
         narration='Before the parser sees anything, an upload over ten thousand characters is refused.'),
    dict(key='28-class-4', kind='code', title='ExpressionEngine — every template can reach the application',
         body='// ExpressionEngine: the first template engine: ${a.b.c} walked by reflection\nMap<String, Object> context = Map.of("customer", customer, "app", app);\n...\nfor (int i = 1; i < parts.length && value != null; i++) {\n    value = method(value, parts[i]).invoke(value);',
         narration='Every template starts from two names, customer and app. [[slnc 300]] Each part of the path calls a method on the value before it. [[slnc 300]] That is how a pasted name reaches the mail password.'),
    dict(key='29-class-5', kind='code', title='ExpressionEngine — any public method will do',
         body='// ExpressionEngine: the first template engine: ${a.b.c} walked by reflection\nfor (Method m : target.getClass().getMethods()) {\n    boolean named = m.getName().equals(name) || m.getName().equals(getter);\n    if (m.getParameterCount() == 0 && named) {\n        return m;',
         narration='The lookup takes any public method with no parameters. [[slnc 300]] Get class is one of them, so the template can reach far beyond the data.'),
    dict(key='30-class-6', kind='code', title='XmlTemplateDemo — the name pasted into the template',
         body='// XmlTemplateDemo: runs the five acts, and makes the mistake behind SSTI\nString injected = "Hello " + mallory.name() + ", your order shipped.";',
         narration="This line is the real mistake. [[slnc 300]] The customer's name becomes part of the template, so the engine treats it as code."),
    dict(key='31-class-7', kind='code', title='LogicLessEngine — a flat list, and escaping',
         body='// LogicLessEngine: the fix: two named holes, escaped values, one pass\nMap<String, String> values = Map.of("name", customer.name(), "email", customer.email());\n...\nm.appendReplacement(out, Matcher.quoteReplacement(value == null ? "" : escape(value)));',
         narration='The fixed engine knows two values, and nothing else. [[slnc 300]] There are no paths and no method calls. [[slnc 300]] Every value is escaped, and the output is never read again.'),
    dict(key='32-outro', kind='outro', title='Thanks for Watching',
         body=['Full source, notes, diagrams and an animated walkthrough', 'are in the repository. Switch off the DOCTYPE refusal', 'and see which other settings still stop the attack.'],
         narration="That's X M L external entities and template injection. [[slnc 400]] If you remember one sentence, make it this one. [[slnc 300]] A parser or an engine that follows instructions found in its input must be told not to, so refuse the doctype, keep templates fixed and logic-less, and pass the customer's text in as data. [[slnc 500]] The full source code, written notes, diagrams, and an animated walkthrough are all in the repository. [[slnc 300]] It runs on your own machine. [[slnc 500]] Here is one exercise to try. [[slnc 300]] Switch off the doctype refusal in the safe parser, and see which of the other settings still stop the file entity. [[slnc 500]] If you found this useful, a like really helps other people discover it. [[slnc 300]] Kindly subscribe to the channel. [[slnc 300]] It helps the channel grow and bring you more content. [[slnc 400]] Thanks for watching!"),
]

VIDEO = {'footer': 'XML External Entities and Template Injection  ·  Security Basics  ·  Java', 'poster': {'headline': [('XXE AND TEMPLATE', 'text'), ('INJECTION', 'accent')], 'taglines': [('A file or a template is a program for its reader', 'gold')], 'before': {'code': '<note>&xxe;</note>', 'note': 'The parser reads a server file', 'tag': 'BEFORE'}, 'after': {'code': 'disallow-doctype-decl', 'note': 'A logic-less engine keeps data as data', 'tag': 'AFTER'}}, 'highlight': {'console_green': ['THE UPLOADS AND RESULTS', 'THE TEMPLATES AND RESULTS', 'THE SAME NAME PASSED AS DATA', 'THE PARSER SETTINGS'], 'console_rose': ['THE TEMPLATE AS BUILT', "THE CUSTOMER'S NAME", 'ANOTHER PASTED NAME'], 'console_amber': ['THE UPLOAD (', 'THE RESULT', "THE OWNER'S TEMPLATE", 'THE NAME ('], 'console_cyan': ['WHAT THE PARSER DOES', 'WHAT THE ENGINE DOES', 'WHAT IT WOULD EXPAND TO', 'HOW THE ENGINE WORKS IT OUT', 'HOW EACH CHARACTER', 'WHAT EVERY TEMPLATE', 'THE VALUES']}}
